record akr.papercut.collated-18-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 18 papercuts from Evidence-intake-project, Lege-ecosystem, SaveYourSkin, jpegXL-rs and 1 more"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 18 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-11 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.i-passed-scope-terms-as-path-src-gui-winsafe-rs [about akr]
        I passed scope terms as "path src/gui/winsafe.rs" to knowledge.propose, copying the `path "..."` form the generated views render, and it was accepted silently — producing scope `path "path src/gui/winsafe.rs"`, a glob that can never match a file, so the records would never have gone stale when winsafe.rs changed. Nothing validates that a scope glob is well-formed or warns that it currently matches zero paths. A warning when a path term matches nothing in the worktree would have caught this at propose time instead of three records later.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-explain-crashed-with-akr-x099 [about akr]
        knowledge.explain crashed with AKR-X099 (internal) for both `decision` and `constraint` after knowledge.propose rejected my slots with AKR-T002. The propose error names the bad slot but not the valid ones, and explain -- the documented way to find them -- is exactly what fails, so I had to read .akr/records/*.akr by hand to learn that a decision uses `decision` plus `claim` blocks and has no `rationale` or `note` slot. Suggest AKR-T002 list the kind's valid slots inline.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-propose-returns-lock-stale-true-on [about akr]
        knowledge.propose returns lock_stale:true on every write but does not refresh akr.lock, so a later knowledge.validate fails with AKR-R052 ("akr.lock has no hash for <the record I just wrote>"). The fix is `akr lock --update`, but nothing in the propose result or the diagnostic says so, and AGENTS.md's "never hand-edit .akr/" made me hesitant to touch the lock at all. Suggest either refreshing the lock as part of propose, or having AKR-R052 name `akr lock --update` as the remedy.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-several-successful-akr-writes-the-mcp [about akr]
        After several successful AKR writes, the MCP transport closed persistently: knowledge.explain and knowledge.revise both failed immediately, and error[AKR-C004]: "D-011" is neither a registered diagnostic code, a known rule, nor a record kind also rejected a decision identifier even though tool guidance names it. The local  fallback completed the handoff update.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-papercut-rejected-its-first-call [about akr]
        `knowledge.papercut` rejected its first call because this multi-namespace project requires an explicit namespace, although the task protocol's example does not mention that requirement. Retrying with `namespace: lege-ecosystem-perf` succeeded.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.after-knowledge-revise-changed-an-existing [about akr]
        After knowledge.revise changed an existing milestone revision from proposed to ready in place, a second revise with the same base revision and state active created a new revision in proposed state instead of activating it. This repeated on revisions 3 and 4; completing directly from ready worked.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.authoring-a-new-track-s-records-cost-three [about akr]
        Authoring a new track's records cost three failed writes to discover relation/slot rules that aren't visible from the propose schema: a `constraint` rejects the `note` slot (planning kinds only, D-026), an `observation` may not declare `supported_by`, and a `milestone` may not declare `implements` (both V-005). The tool description lists relation names generically, so the per-kind restrictions only surface as errors after a full record body is composed. Either the propose schema's relations field could name the allowed relations per kind, or the V-005 error could suggest the nearest legal relation (`derived_from` in both of my cases). Separately, an `observation`'s `observed_at` requires a 40-hex commit while the kind's description just says "observed_at", so an ISO date is a natural first guess and fails with a parse cascade of three diagnostics.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-context-rejected-a-valid-key-revision [about akr]
        knowledge.context rejected a valid @key/revision reference even though knowledge.get accepts that canonical reference form; it required the bare logical key, making goal resumption take two retries. The context tool/docs could state or normalize this syntax.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-supersede-documents-a-new-key-option [about akr]
        knowledge.supersede documents a new_key option, but AKR 0.1 rejects every different-key supersession with AKR-C004. I had to supersede the existing key in place, which prevents giving a materially changed design ruling a more accurate key.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.revising-an-active-decision-s-content [about akr]
        Revising an active decision's content implicitly returned its lifecycle state to proposed, requiring a second state-only revise. Preserving the head state by default, or explicitly warning that omitted state resets it, would avoid an easy accidental deactivation.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-removing-37-acknowledged-missing-source [about akr]
        While removing 37 acknowledged missing-source citations, knowledge.get, knowledge.revise, knowledge.explain, and knowledge.validate repeatedly returned Transport closed; the local akr CLI remained healthy and provided the necessary fallback.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-documents-observation [about akr]
        knowledge.propose documents observation observed_at as required but does not say it must be a git:<40-hex> locator; passing the natural ISO date 2026-08-11 produced parser errors about a 4-digit commit hash.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-says-observation-requires [about akr]
        knowledge.propose says observation requires statement and observed_at, but a verified observation also requires method/source/evidence (V-022); after adding method, the natural accompanying command slot is rejected because observation does not permit command.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-explain-assessment-lists-optional-as-of-but [about akr]
        akr explain assessment lists optional as_of but not that it requires a git commit; using an ISO date caused a safe parse failure. Showing slot types in explain would avoid this retry.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.akr-propose-from-rejected-a-prose-body-as-does [about akr]
        akr propose --from rejected a prose body as 'does not parse as a record'; the CLI help calls it a body source but this build requires a complete canonical record.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-explain-observation-and-knowledge [about akr]
        knowledge.explain observation and knowledge.papercut both failed with Transport closed while recording the sky-stage diagnosis; the local akr CLI worked as a fallback.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-akr-cli-search-syntax-differs-from-the-mcp [about akr]
        The AKR CLI search syntax differs from the MCP shape: --query is rejected and the help must be consulted separately.

        ## raw-autotune @raw-autotune.papercut.the-knowledge-context-mcp-connector-returned [about akr]
        The knowledge.context MCP connector returned 'Transport closed' at the start of implementation; using the equivalent akr CLI workflow.
        """
    observed_at git:03e4af3c2e62cb07ab00436e512bedc41cd88436
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.i-passed-scope-terms-as-path-src-gui-winsafe-rs",
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-explain-crashed-with-akr-x099",
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-propose-returns-lock-stale-true-on",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-several-successful-akr-writes-the-mcp",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-papercut-rejected-its-first-call",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.after-knowledge-revise-changed-an-existing",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.authoring-a-new-track-s-records-cost-three",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-context-rejected-a-valid-key-revision",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-supersede-documents-a-new-key-option",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.revising-an-active-decision-s-content",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.while-removing-37-acknowledged-missing-source",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-documents-observation",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-says-observation-requires",
        "raw-autotune.papercut.akr-explain-assessment-lists-optional-as-of-but",
        "raw-autotune.papercut.akr-propose-from-rejected-a-prose-body-as-does",
        "raw-autotune.papercut.knowledge-explain-observation-and-knowledge",
        "raw-autotune.papercut.the-akr-cli-search-syntax-differs-from-the-mcp",
        "raw-autotune.papercut.the-knowledge-context-mcp-connector-returned"
